  "parameter_rationale": {
    "road_legality": "Exact Driving membership remains the offroad check. R7 separately uses CARLA waypoint adjacency, lane-change permission and direction alignment; a Broken sensor event alone never legalizes an opposing-lane crossing.",
    "junction_scope": "The registered Town05 R7 train/evaluation pools use straight road segments. Junction waypoint ambiguity is nonterminal but success-ineligible; any future goal inside a junction or route crossing road identities requires a newly versioned route-legality protocol and live tests.",
    "lane_reward": "Legal old-lane following and legal new-lane following share the same zero-cost deadzone. Legal lane changes receive neither bonus nor event cost; progress remains the only positive dense reward.",
    "critic": "R6 reached the coupled 5 percent critic learning-rate floor before stable value fit. R7 holds critic lr through update 300, then decays only to 1e-4 while recording pooled, agent, outcome and scenario fit evidence plus a bounded checkpoint probe.",
    "horizon": "The 600-update horizon separates early exploration, critic fitting and late policy refinement. Milestones are safe checkpoints, not claims of convergence.",
    "compatibility": "R7 is fresh-only schema-v7 with reward v5 and new metrics/outcome contracts. R6 schema-v6 checkpoints and the failed R6 run remain historical evidence and cannot resume or enter the R7 policy pool.",
    "observation": "Actor and centralized critic input dimensions stay at the R6 20-dimensional time-aware observation contract; road legality is never added to either observation.",
    "scope": "Actors remain independent and behavior cloning remains disabled so road/reward/critic changes stay attributable; shared actor and BC remain P1 ablations."
  }
